      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should this case also be considered a failure?\n\nI\u0027m not necessarily arguing that this case _is_ a failure. But, if it\u0027s not, I\u0027d like to understand when callers should expect a failure callback, vs. when they should not. With the code as-is, it seems like there are three possible outcomes:\n- caller gets Success callback\n- caller gets Failure callback\n- caller gets no callback\n\nIs that as intended?",
      "revId": "caf1a21dd265f4e3d92449c4fb16c2efa28595f5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9fd85cb1_aa41eff5",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/wifi_chip.cpp",
